## 1. Introduction
In the past few years, perovskite solar cells (PSCs) based on organic–inorganic hybrid metal triiodide perovskite (MTP) materials (e.g., methylammonia lead iodide $\left(\mathbf{MAPbI}_{3}\right)_{.}^{\cdot}$ ) have been considered to be one of the most promising types of third-generation solar cells (SCs). This is mainly because their power conversion efficiencies (PCEs) have reached over $20\%$ , starting from $3.8\%$ in 2009.1–6 Compared to the traditional commercialized SCs, it is very impressive to obtain such a high
